                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Henry Siddons, actor and playwright, (1774-1815) was the eldest child of William and <persName key="SID01">Sarah Siddons</persName>. See his entry in <title>DNB</title>.
    He first appears in the diary in 1796 with C Kemble, taken to be Charles Kemble, Siddons' uncle. 
    He dines with Godwin at Reynold's in 1803 and then does not appear again  until 1807 where he is noted in five entries between 14 November and 12
    December - Godwin writes to him and there follows a series of calls.</p>
